  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "Scope is `**/*.razor` and its `**/*.razor.cs` code-behind. `.cshtml` MVC views and Razor Pages belong to omega-framework-asp-net-core, and `@section` -- which only `.cshtml` accepts -- is therefore not matched here.",
      "A parameter's declared type is not reachable: omega-razor spans `reference.attribute` on the attribute and `definition.declared_type_candidate` on the whole property declaration, and `fact_join_by_span` only reaches a fact that CONTAINS the current one, so the marker can reach the property but nothing can reach the property's type from the marker.",
      "The event a markup binding fires is not reachable: omega-razor publishes the razor attribute name (`onclick`, `bind-Value`) as the ATTRIBUTE `attribute` on `reference.attribute_value`, and an attribute can only be compared to one literal constant. The handler method is stated; which DOM event calls it is not.",
      "A navigation target is not reachable: `NavigationManager.NavigateTo(\"/counter\")` arrives as `call.method NavigateTo` with no argument text, and `<a href=\"/counter\">` is plain markup omega-razor does not emit at all. Literal-href and NavigateTo routing edges are therefore absent.",
      "Component usage in markup (`<Counter Title=\"x\" />`) is not emitted by omega-razor, so which component renders which other component is unanswerable; only the layout edge from `@layout` survives.",
